---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "September 15, 2026";
const CONTACT_EMAIL = "hello@digitaldramaa.com";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — DigitalDramaa"
  description="How DigitalDramaa collects, uses, and protects information when you use the site."
  keywords={["DigitalDramaa", "privacy policy", "digitaldramaa privacy"]}
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      This policy explains what information DigitalDramaa ("we", "us") collects
      when you visit digitaldramaa.com (the "Site"), and how it's used. By using
      the Site, you agree to the practices described here.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We don't require an account to read or listen to articles. The information we handle is limited to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Local preferences.</strong> Your theme choice (light/dark) and
        whether you've dismissed the announcement banner are stored in your
        browser's local storage. This data never leaves your device and isn't
        sent to us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Standard server logs.</strong> Our hosting and content-delivery
        providers automatically log basic technical data for every request —
        things like IP address, browser type, and page requested — for
        security and reliability purposes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Voice playback requests.</strong> When you request audio
        playback of an article, the article text is sent to our text-to-speech
        provider to generate speech on demand. The resulting audio may be
        cached so future requests for the same article don't need to
        regenerate it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>
      We use the data above to operate, secure, and improve the Site — for
      example, detecting abuse, diagnosing errors, and understanding overall
      traffic patterns. We do not sell personal information, and we don't use
      the data above to build advertising profiles.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies & Local Storage</h2>
    <p>
      The Site uses browser local storage (not tracking cookies) to remember
      your theme preference and banner dismissal. You can clear this at any
      time through your browser's settings without affecting your ability to
      use the Site.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      The Site relies on a handful of third-party services to function:
      hosting and content-delivery infrastructure, a database provider for
      storing articles, a text-to-speech provider for on-demand audio, and
      Google Fonts for typography. Each of these providers may process
      standard technical/request data as part of delivering their service,
      subject to their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>
      Every article links back to the original source it was based on. Those
      sites are operated independently of DigitalDramaa, and we aren't
      responsible for their content or privacy practices. We encourage you to
      review the privacy policy of any third-party site you visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Server logs and cached audio are retained only as long as needed for the
      operational purposes described above, after which they are deleted or
      allowed to expire in the ordinary course of business.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
      reflected by updating the effective date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or via our
      <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: var(--sp-32) 0 var(--sp-24);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-32);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--note);
    background: var(--note-wash);
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
  }

  .page-head p {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 72ch;
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-64);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: var(--sp-32) 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .prose h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: var(--sp-24);
  }

  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
